translation:
Emaho!
First, as for how the eight names of the Guru appeared:
I establish the sentient beings of the three realms in bliss;
I am Guru Padma 'byung-gnas.
I am the sovereign of the teachings, the Lord of Dharma;
I am Guru Padma saṃbhava.
Untainted by flaws and embodying the three pitakas;
I am Guru Padma rgyal-po.
All bliss is perfected within my body;
I am Guru Rdo-rje gro-lod.
All vehicles are equalized, pervading like space;
I am Guru Nyi-ma 'od-zer.
Within a single body, the eight manifestations are displayed;
I am Guru Śākya seng-ge.
Proclaiming the sound of Dharma to all the six realms;
I am Guru Seng-ge sgra-sgrog.
Knowing all that can be known;
I am Guru Blo-ldan mchog-sred.
This is the first chapter, on the Eight Manifestations of the Guru.

Emaho!
Tenth, the presentation of the eight disciples who uphold the Dharma lineage:
Namkhai Nyingpo, who rides upon the rays of the sun;
Sangye Yeshe, who drives his kīla into solid rock;
Ngenlam Gyalchok, who intones the melody of the horse's neigh;
Yeshe Tsogyal, who revives the corpses of the slain;
Drogmi Palgyi, who brings the mamos into servitude;
Who brings the arrogant lions and elephants under his power;
Vairotsana, who is equal to the Orgyen himself;
And the Sovereign King, who is able to manifest emanations.
This is the tenth chapter, on the eight disciples who display emanations.

Emaho!
Twelfth, the presentation of the eight ladies who captured my heart:
The Indian princess Mandāravā;
The gifted woman Yeshé Tsogyal;
The one of perfect service, Chogroza Shélsgrön;
The one of perfect faith, Margyenza Tsho;
The one of perfect realization, Shéldkar Tségrön;
The four royal sisters, the princesses;
The one of perfect attainment, Princess Tröma Gyen;
The King’s beloved, Princess Pema Sel;
The Queen’s beloved, the power-bestowing Salé.
This is the twelfth chapter, on the eight consorts.

Emaho!
Thirteenth, the presentation of the eight enlightened activities:
Unattached to samsara, I engaged in various playful displays;
Equal to all the Buddhas, I displayed various miraculous feats;
Through the conduct of yogic discipline, I performed the practice of the corpse;
Teaching the Dharma to beings, I acted as their mother and father;
Having vanquished the hosts of Māra, I acted as a Buddha and Bodhisattva;
Having vanquished the hosts of Māra, I acted as a Buddha and Bodhisattva;
Having turned the wheel of Dharma, I set foot in the land of Tibet;
Having caused the teachings to flourish, I concealed precious treasures;
Having suppressed the rākṣasas, I established the world in bliss.
This is the thirteenth chapter, on the eight enlightened activities.

Emaho!
Fourteenth, the presentation of the eight hidden treasure caches:
Considering the timing, I concealed mind treasures;
Upon being seen or heard, I concealed secret treasures that bring certainty;
I concealed profound treasures as symbolic scripts on yellow parchment;
I concealed rediscovered treasures that are wondrous and marvelous;
To protect against poverty, I concealed wealth treasures;
To tame various beings in myriad ways, I concealed minor treasures;
I concealed two treasures that are not fixed in a single form;
To protect the precious teachings, I concealed mind treasures.
This is the fourteenth chapter, on the eight hidden treasure caches.

Emaho!
Sixteenth, the presentation of the eight Lingpas who are Lords of the Dharma:
They are emanations of the eight great Bodhisattvas.
In the center is Orgyen Lingpa;
In the east is Dorje Lingpa;
In the south is Rinchen Lingpa;
In the west is Pema Lingpa;
In the north is Karma Lingpa;
Samten Ling and Nyida Ling,
Zhikpo Ling and Terdak Ling;
These eight great treasure-revealing Lingpas will appear,
And they are certainly emanations of me, Orgyen.
This is the sixteenth chapter, on the eight Lingpas who are Lords of the Dharma.

Emaho!
Great King, listen well.
One such as I, Padmasambhava,
Possess the five common clairvoyances,
The five clairvoyances of the future,
The five clairvoyances of the present,
And the five immeasurable clairvoyances;
These five types of clairvoyance are known to me.
In former times, I was Amitābha, Boundless Light;
On Mount Potala, I was the Protector Avalokiteśvara;
At Dhanakośa, I was the form of Padmasambhava.
Although appearing as three merely as a mode of manifestation,
In reality, they are inseparable and not distinct from one another.
In the realm of the Dharmadhātu, I am Samantabhadra;
In the Dense Array, I am the Great Vajradhara;
At the Vajra Seat, I am the Great Sage himself;
Non-dual with them, I, Padma, am spontaneously present.
Therefore, pray to me constantly.
